│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a simple linear chain of CZ gates. This modification introduces   │
│                          │ more entanglement by using interleaved patterns of CZ gates across odd and even qubit     │
│                          │ pairs. This approach increases circuit expressivity without significantly increasing      │
│                          │ depth, potentially improving accuracy and reducing the train-test gap by allowing better  │
│                          │ exploration of the parameter space.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The changes include:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Replacing the linear CZ chain with two interleaved layers of CZ gates (odd-even        │
│                          │ pattern)                                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Adding parameterized single-qubit rotations before and after the entangling layers to  │
│                          │ increase expressivity                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Maintaining the data re-uploading structure but enhancing the ansatz block with more   │
│                          │ sophisticated entanglement                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This modification should improve the model's ability to learn complex feature             │
│                          │ correlations while keeping the parameter count reasonable.                                │
