│ patch_description        │ The current model uses independent parameters for every gate, leading to 146 parameters   │
│                          │ and potential overfitting, as evidenced by the high train accuracy (1.00) and slightly    │
│                          │ lower test accuracy (0.98). I will implement a parameter-sharing scheme (grouping by      │
│                          │ qubit parity) that reduces the number of unique parameters per ansatz block from 24 to 6, │
│                          │ significantly improving parameter efficiency. Additionally, I will replace the linear     │
│                          │ CZ-chain entanglement with a more expressive connectivity pattern (inspired by the seed   │
│                          │ program's structure), which should maintain high accuracy while potentially allowing for  │
│                          │ faster convergence and better generalization by utilizing circuit depth more effectively. │
