│ patch_name               │ crx_ring_evolution                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The successful "CRX chain" architecture demonstrated that controlled rotations (CRX)      │
│                          │ provide significantly better expressivity for this task compared to fixed CZ gates. The   │
│                          │ "CRX ring" configuration (connecting all qubits in a cyclic fashion) performed            │
│                          │ exceptionally well in the prior experiments (reaching score 1.52).                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ In this evolution, I am combining the structural robustness of the previous               │
│                          │ high-performing CRX-chain model with a refined parameter strategy. Specifically:          │
│                          │ 1. Retain the "RY layer" to allow flexible amplitude encoding.                            │
│                          │ 2. Use the "CRX chain" configuration as the primary entangler to allow data-dependent     │
│                          │ control over qubit phases, which effectively captures the correlations in the             │
│                          │ 28-dimensional binary feature space.                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Replace the simple trailing RZ layer with a more efficient parameter-shared RZ layer   │
│                          │ to slightly reduce the parameter count while maintaining the necessary phase-tuning       │
│                          │ capacity.                                                                                 │
│                          │ This configuration balances model capacity (expressivity of CRX) with parameter           │
│                          │ efficiency, aiming for a faster convergence and lower generalization gap.                 │
