│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ switchtocxringspec                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 27 trainable parameters per block (RY 8 + RZ-pre 8 + CRZ 3 +      │
│                          │ RZ-post 8), which leads to 164 total parameters (27 * 6 + readout). In prior trials, a    │
│                          │ simpler “RY + CRX ring + RZ” structure achieved perfect/generalization performance with   │
│                          │ 24 parameters per block (146 total) and a better combined score.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ So, replace the current CZ/CRZ scaffold with an 8-parameter CRX ring (one CRX per         │
│                          │ adjacent pair in a cycle), while keeping the per-qubit RY and per-qubit RZ (pre-encoding  │
│                          │ basis). This reduces parameters and matches the stronger mixing inductive bias seen in    │
│                          │ the earlier high-scoring program, while remaining fully compatible with the fixed feature │
│                          │ map and re-upload schedule.                                                               │
