│ patch_description        │ I implemented a hybrid entanglement strategy to improve efficiency and reduce the         │
│                          │ train-test gap. By replacing fully parameterized CRX ring layers—which often suffer from  │
│                          │ redundant expressivity or excessive depth when parameters are shared—with a mixture of    │
│                          │ fixed CZ gates and parameterized CRX gates, the circuit achieves a more robust landscape. │
│                          │ Specifically, even-indexed edges (0-1, 2-3, etc.) use fixed CZ gates to provide           │
│                          │ non-parameterized correlation, while odd-indexed edges (1-2, 3-4, etc.) use CRX gates to  │
│                          │ inject learnable phase-rotation conditional on control states. This structural variation  │
│                          │ helps reduce the gate count and depth while maintaining high classification capability.   │
