│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ leaning_crx_ring_with_cz_seed                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current over-parameterized ansatz block (which uses extra pre/post Z layers   │
│                          │ and only three CRZ gates) with a simpler, higher-capacity-per-parameter structure         │
│                          │ inspired by the stronger prior candidates:                                                │
│                          │ - Keep an initial layer of single-qubit RY on all 8 qubits.                               │
│                          │ - Use the same fixed CZ “pairs” as in the previous best patterns.                         │
│                          │ - Add a ring-style set of 4 parameterized CRX gates (one per entangling edge), using      │
│                          │ fewer parameters than the current CRZ+extra RZ layers.                                    │
│                          │ - Finish with a full single-qubit RZ layer on all 8 qubits.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 27 → 20 (so N_PARAMS from 164 → 122 under the fixed  │
│                          │ training loop), while increasing entangling expressivity (CRX ring) relative to the       │
│                          │ current CRZ-only middle layer.                                                            │
